  "timing": "Five shuffled repetitions of each variant/case, with separate instrumented profiles. Includes model/IR/workspace preparation, search and witness return; excludes compilation/loading, warmups and independent validation. No concurrent CPU-heavy jobs.",
  "policies": {
    "bounds": "Incremental sorted-rank contribution bounds, reconciled on widening; cached global extrema. Bounds passes revisit until fixpoint.",
    "staged": "Exact equality supports when active <=2, or active <=4 and active candidates <=64; otherwise bounds.",
    "budget": "Exact equality supports when active <=2 or active candidates * (min(target-lower,upper-target)//64+1) <=20000; otherwise bounds. The estimate is heuristic, not an execution limit.",
    "delta": "Canonical masks updated from candidate deltas; graph and transpose updated from changed arcs and validated current matching. Reachability and SCC still fully recomputed.",
    "shared": "One authoritative C domain array; propagation and branch writes trail immediately; incremental sizes; sparse rollback snapshots preserve initial queue order."
  },
  "caveats": [
    "Exploratory selected seed/settings, not held-out general solver ranking",
    "Gecode uses different branching/value randomness, propagation algorithms and node counting; no universal speed claim",
    "Bounds-only and narrow staged policies regress sharply on completed smaller cases",
    "Budget policy improves measured 16/20 but regresses on 9; no production default changes",
    "Exact baseline/delta/shared ablations preserve search, reductions and work digests; weaker policies can change search",
    "Budget and exact have identical recorded 20 random-order work, not guaranteed equivalence on all inputs",
    "POSIX C11 native feasibility subset, no objectives/rules/hybrid residual search",
    "Legacy Python presets unchanged; new native settings saved separately"
  ]
